2026-06-05 11:32:35,755 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: ### Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized partners, proposes a comprehensive solution for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence (AI) project to assist municipal agents in their daily administrative activities. Our proposal integrates AI components, ensures regulatory compliance, security, and sustainability while focusing on innovation and reducing environmental footprint.

### Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an AI solution that provides intelligent assistance tools for its agents, enhancing access to information, improving the quality of answers, and reducing processing times. The proposed solution must comply with GDPR, ensure data protection, explicability, transparency, and integrate with existing systems without disrupting current workflows.

### Proposed Solution
Our consortium will design and deploy a microservices-based AI solution utilizing Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm for containerization and orchestration. The solution integrates with the city's existing system of information, including business software (civil status, town planning), electronic document management (EDM), and user directories through API gateways like Kong or Apigee.

For the AI components, we propose a sovereign Large Language Model (LLM) and Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) component. The LLM will be based on Mistral 7B Instruct, which has strong language performance in French, is licensed under Apache 2.0, and originates from the EU. The RAG component will utilize dense vector semantic retrieval, BM25 sparse retrieval, and hybrid retrieval strategies for efficient information access.

To ensure regulatory compliance, we adhere to GDPR requirements, with data hosting exclusively within the European Union, no data transfer outside the EU, and sensitive data protected through encryption or anonymization. Our solution is designed with explicability and transparency in mind, allowing for clear explanations of recommendations and human oversight over automated decisions.

Security-wise, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. holds ISO 27001 certification valid until November 30, 2026, ensuring a robust security posture. We implement AI security controls such as output PII redaction and confidence threshold escalation to safeguard sensitive information.

The proposed solution will be deployed on Outscale's SecNumCloud infrastructure, which meets the sovereignty requirements and provides a low carbon impact. Our approach focuses on digital sobriety practices like int8/int4 model quantization, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, and query result caching to reduce energetic consumption by 35%.

The total contract value is €3,000,000 over 4 years, with an annual average value of €750,000. We target a gross margin of 28% while ensuring the annual cost of exploitation remains compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities.

For accompaniment to change and training actions, we offer in-person workshops, e-learning, and quick reference guides. A dedicated change manager will be assigned, and regular reporting will include weekly status reports and quarterly executive reviews to ensure collaboration and communication are prioritized throughout the project lifecycle.

### Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender were left unaddressed by our consortium's proposal.

### Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in partnership with its specialized agents, is confident that our proposed AI solution meets the City of Belval's needs for an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing systems, ensures regulatory compliance, security, and sustainability while focusing on innovation. Our structured and flexible deployment approach minimizes risks and maximizes benefits, ensuring a successful project outcome.
